      "slug": "double-treble",
      "term": "Double treble",
      "definition": "UK: dtr. Two yarn-overs before inserting the hook. Four pairs of loops worked off two at a time. Twice the height of a regular treble."
    },
    {
      "slug": "turning-chain",
      "term": "Turning chain",
      "definition": "Four chains at the start of each double treble row, counting as the first dtr."
    },
